/**
# Functional Helpers

Builtins that transform any **iterable** — arrays, dicts, strings, bytes,
ranges, key-value arrays and the iterators these helpers return — without an
explicit loop. `map`, `filter`, `keys`, `values`, `items`, `enumerate` and `zip`
are **lazy**: they return an iterator that does the work as it is consumed, by
`collect` (into an array), a `for … in` loop or another helper. `reduce` and
`each` run at once. Part of the [Collections](collections.gad) chapter; the
iterator protocol for your own types is in [Control Flow](control_flow.gad).

## map and filter

`map(it, cb)` yields `cb(value, key)` for each element — the key is the index,
or the dict key. With the `nokey` flag the callback takes only the value.
`filter(it, cb)` keeps the elements for which `cb(value, key, it)` is truthy.
Both return iterators, so they chain.

@snippet map_filter

`map(…; update)` also writes each result back into the collection — as the
iterator is consumed, since it is lazy:

@snippet map_update

## reduce and each

`reduce(it, cb, initial)` folds the elements into one value, calling
`cb(accumulator, value, key)` and keeping what it returns; without `initial` the
first element starts the fold. `each(it, cb)` calls `cb(key, value)` — **key
first**, unlike `map`/`filter` — for its side effects and returns the iterable.

@snippet reduce_each

## keys, values, items and enumerate

`keys` and `values` iterate one side of a collection; `items` yields its
entries as key-value pairs `[(key)=value]` (`.k` / `.v`), and `enumerate` pairs
each element with its position the same way.

@snippet entries

## zip, iterate and toArray

`zip(a, b, …)` **chains** its iterables end to end (it does not pair them).
`iterate(x)` returns a plain iterator over any iterable. `toArray(…)`
concatenates its arguments into one array — an array contributes its elements,
another iterable its `[(key)=value]` entries.

@snippet chain_convert

## sort and sortReverse

`sort` / `sortReverse` return the collection ordered ascending / descending; a
`less=(a, b) => …` comparator customises the order.

@snippet sorting

## A pipeline

Chained, the lazy helpers read as a pipeline: nothing runs until `collect` asks
for values, and each element flows through every stage before the next one
starts.

@snippet pipeline
**/

//snippet map_filter
nums := [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
[
    collect(map(nums, (v, i) => v * 10 + i)),           // value, index
    collect(map(nums, (v) => v * v; nokey)),            // value only
    collect(filter(nums, (v, i, all) => v % 2 == 1)),   // value, index, iterable
    collect(map({a: 1}, (v, k) => k + "=" + str(v))),   // a dict: value, key
    collect(filter("gad lang", (c, i, s) => c != ' ')), // a string: its chars
]
/**= [[10, 21, 32, 43, 54], [1, 4, 9, 16, 25], [1, 3, 5], ["a=1"], ['g', 'a', 'd', 'l', 'a', 'n', 'g']] **/
//endsnippet

//snippet map_update
prices := [10, 20]
lazy := map(prices, (v, i) => v * 2; update)
before := copy(prices)             // nothing ran yet
collect(lazy)                      // consuming it writes the results back
[before, prices]
/**= [[10, 20], [20, 40]] **/
//endsnippet

//snippet reduce_each
total := reduce([1, 2, 3, 4], (acc, v, i) => acc + v, 0)
longest := reduce(["go", "gad", "lang"], (acc, v, i) => len(v) > len(acc) ? v : acc)
seen := []
each({x: 1}, (k, v) => { seen += k + str(v) })   // key first
[total, longest, seen, typeName(each([1], (i, v) => nil))]
/**= [10, "lang", ["x1"], "array"] **/
//endsnippet

//snippet entries
d := {name: "gad"}
pair := collect(items(d))[0]
[
    collect(keys(d)), collect(values(["x", "y"])),
    [pair.k, pair.v],
    [[e.k, e.v] for e in enumerate(["a", "b"])],
]
/**= [["name"], ["x", "y"], ["name", "gad"], [[0, "a"], [1, "b"]]] **/
//endsnippet

//snippet chain_convert
[
    collect(zip([1, 2], ["a"], 3 .. 4)),   // chained, not paired
    collect(iterate("ab")),
    toArray([1, 2], [3]),                  // arrays: their elements
    [[e.k, e.v] for e in toArray("ab")],   // other iterables: their entries
]
/**= [[1, 2, "a", 3, 4], ['a', 'b'], [1, 2, 3], [[0, 'a'], [1, 'b']]] **/
//endsnippet

//snippet sorting
[
    sort([3, 1, 2]),
    sortReverse([3, 1, 2]),
    sort(["pear", "fig", "apple"]; less=(a, b) => len(a) < len(b)),
]
/**= [[1, 2, 3], [3, 2, 1], ["fig", "pear", "apple"]] **/
//endsnippet

//snippet pipeline
squaresOfEvens := map(
    filter(1 .. 10, (v, i, r) => v % 2 == 0),
    (v) => v * v; nokey,
)
[typeName(squaresOfEvens), collect(squaresOfEvens), reduce(squaresOfEvens, (a, v, i) => a + v, 0)]
/**= ["MapIterator", [4, 16, 36, 64, 100], 220] **/
//endsnippet
